d_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: Several pods show non-zero restart counts (e.g., `geo-57c7bd6d5c-6pkff` with 3 restarts, `profile-69cb98cb67-r7r4p` with 2 restarts). To investigate potential crashes or errors, I need to retrieve logs from these pods to identify specific failure reasons (e.g., crashes, configuration errors, dependency issues). This will help pinpoint the root cause of the restarts.  \n\n**Target pods for logs**:  \n- `geo-57c7bd6d5c-6pkff`  \n- `profile-69cb98cb67-r7r4p`  \n- `rate-6fff88f6f5-5pdc7`  \n- `recommendation-64754c9c4f-h28hq`  \n- `reservation-7bb77b596b-zstn7`  \n- `user-6548d868cd-gpdgl`  \n\nI'll start by checking logs for the `geo` pod, which has the highest restart count.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 563, 'prompt_tokens': 4073, 'total_tokens': 4636, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cff32-18d1-7470-b439-227faef76c8c-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4073, 'output_tokens': 563, 'total_tokens': 4636}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='ff64e3cd-221f-475f-9697-59c27aa32dc5'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose issues in a hotel reservation application with multiple microservices. So far, they\'ve checked the services, deployments, and pods, and noticed some pods have restarts. The next step is to look into the logs of those pods to find out why they\'re restarting.\n\nThe user mentioned the geo pod has 3 restarts, so they should check its logs first. The tool available is exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd, which can run kubectl commands. The command to get logs is kubectl logs <pod-name> -n <