namespace>. \n\nWait, but the user needs to specify the pod name. The previous output listed the pod names, so the geo pod is geo-57c7bd6d5c-6pkff. The namespace is hotel-reservation. So the command should be kubectl logs geo-57c7bd6d5c-6pkff -n hotel-reservation. \n\nBut the tool\'s parameters require the command to start with "kubectl". So the correct command is "kubectl logs geo-57c7bd6d5c-6pkff -n hotel-reservation". That should retrieve the logs for the geo pod. Let me make sure there are no typos in the pod name. Yes, that\'s the one with 3 restarts. This will help identify any errors or crashes causing the restarts.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs geo-57c7bd6d5c-6pkff -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-bac7b03f660edc20', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 341, 'prompt_tokens': 5235, 'total_tokens': 5576, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cff32-3351-72b2-8e1b-7610aa322c60-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs geo-57c7bd6d5c-6pkff -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-bac7b03f660edc20', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5235, 'output_tokens': 341, 'total_tokens': 5576}), ToolMessage(content='{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-18T04:25:14Z","message":"TLS disabled."}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-18T04:25:14Z","message":"Set global log level: info"}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-18T04:25:14Z","message":"Tune: setGCPercent to 100"}\n\x1b[90m2026-03-18T04:25:14Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/geo/main.go:23\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mReading config...\x1b[0m