 steps, they used \'get_services\' and \'get_deployments\', but not \'get_traces\' yet. Maybe using \'get_traces\' for the \'geo\' service to see if there are any traces that are failing. But the user hasn\'t done that yet. Alternatively, checking the metrics for the \'geo\' service to see if there are any errors.\n\nBut the user\'s last action was checking the logs for \'geo\', which didn\'t show errors. So maybe the next step is to check the logs for another pod, like \'profile\', which also had restarts. Let\'s see, the \'profile\' pod\'s logs might show why it\'s restarting. So the user should call \'kubectl logs\' for \'profile-69cb98cb67-r7r4p\' to check for errors. But the user can only use the available tools, which include \'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd\'. So the next tool call should be to get the logs of the \'profile\' pod.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The `geo` pod logs appear normal, but it had 3 restarts. I\'ll now check the `profile` pod (with 2 restarts) to see if it has similar or different issues. This will help determine if the problem is isolated to `geo` or part of a broader pattern.  \n**Target pod**: `profile-69cb98cb67-r7r4p`', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 972, 'prompt_tokens': 5879, 'total_tokens': 6851, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cff32-4724-7903-93c3-58874e4cb96a-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5879, 'output_tokens': 972, 'total_tokens': 6851}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='53934773-277e-422a-aef7-181e6f6a069e'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagn