The user needs to add the correct environment variables to the deployments for geo, profile, and rate. These variables should point to the MongoDB services (mongodb-geo, mongodb-profile, mongodb-rate) using the appropriate URLs or hostnames. Once that's done, the services should be able to connect to the databases, and the restarts should stop. 

I should confirm that the MongoDB services are correctly named and accessible. Also, check if there are any network policies or firewall rules blocking the connections. But based on the current info, the main issue is the missing environment variables in the deployments.
