end                 1/1     1            1           3m8s\ngeo                      1/1     1            1           3m8s\njaeger                   1/1     1            1           3m5s\nmemcached-profile        1/1     1            1           3m1s\nmemcached-rate           1/1     1            1           2m56s\nmemcached-reserve        1/1     1            1           2m42s\nmongodb-geo              1/1     1            1           3m6s\nmongodb-profile          1/1     1            1           3m\nmongodb-rate             1/1     1            1           2m53s\nmongodb-recommendation   1/1     1            1           2m49s\nmongodb-reservation      1/1     1            1           2m40s\nmongodb-user             1/1     1            1           2m31s\nprofile                  1/1     1            1           2m58s\nrate                     1/1     1            1           2m52s\nrecommendation           1/1     1            1           2m46s\nreservation              1/1     1            1           2m37s\nsearch                   1/1     1            1           2m35s\nuser                     1/1     1            1           2m30s\n', id='ded82b10-6561-424d-8f88-581d23e92f47', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-84a13fd0e599ab8e'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='95d4c132-be3f-4cfc-8275-eb96edd8c1b6'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose a hotel reservation application with many microservices. So far, they\'ve checked the services and deployments, and all the deployments are showing as healthy (READY, UP-TO-DATE, AVAILABLE). But the problem is that some or none of the microservices might have faults. Since the deployments are all okay, maybe the issue is not with the deployment configurations but something else.\n\nNext step: Check the pods to see if any are not running or have errors. Even