 \nreasoning: The `geo` deployment's container environment variables only include `JAEGER_SAMPLE_RATIO`, with no MongoDB connection details (e.g., `MONGODB_URL`, `MONGODB_PROFILE`, etc.). This confirms a critical misconfiguration: the services `geo`, `profile`, and `rate` lack environment variables to connect to their respective MongoDB instances (`mongodb-geo`, `mongodb-profile`, `mongodb-rate`). Without these, the services cannot establish database connections, leading to crashes and restarts.  \n**Command**: `kubectl get deployment profile -n hotel-reservation -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].env}'` (repeat for `rate` deployment)", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 464, 'prompt_tokens': 18090, 'total_tokens': 18554, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cff34-f683-7f63-a0fb-86032d832fb2-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 18090, 'output_tokens': 464, 'total_tokens': 18554}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='01d1e4b6-a8d3-4902-867f-68123484af34'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what's going on here. The user is trying to diagnose why some microservices in the hotel-reservation application are restarting. They've already checked the pods, deployments, and logs, but haven't found the root cause. \n\nFrom the previous steps, they noticed that the geo, profile, and rate pods have multiple restarts. They checked the logs and didn't see obvious errors, but the metrics queries didn't show any errors either. Then they looked into the deployment configurations and found that the environment variables for these services are missing MongoDB connection details. \n\nThe key insight here is that the services are supposed to connect to MongoDB instances like mongodb-geo, mongodb-profile, etc., but the environment variables that hold these connection strings are missing. Without these, the services can't connect to the databases, leading to crashes and restarts. \n\nThe user tried to check the deployment configurations for the geo service and saw that only JAEGER_SAMPLE_RATIO is set. The same applies to the profile and rate deployments. This confirms that the MongoDB connection details are not properly configured in the deployments. \n\nThe next step would be to check the deployment YAML files to see if the environment variables for MongoDB are missing. But since the user can't edit files directly, they might need to use kubectl to get the full deployment configuration. However, the available tools don't include a way to get the full YAML, so they might have to infer based on the existing commands. \n\nSince the user has already confirmed that the environment variables are missing, the root cause is clear: the deployments for geo, profile, and rate don't have the necessary environment variables to connect to their respective MongoDB instances. This leads to the services failing to start or crashing, causing the restarts. \n\nThe final answer should state that the root cause is the absence of MongoDB connection environment variables in the deployments, leading to connection failures and restarts.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get deployment profile -n hotel-reservation -o jsonpath=\'{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].env}\'"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8afd013124085310', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 443, 'prompt_tokens': 19145, 'total_tokens': 19588, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cff35-0f10-79d3-b546-b64ec56a7010-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': "kubectl get deployment profile -n hotel-reservation -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].env}'"}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8afd013124085310', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 19145, 'output_tokens': 443, 'total_tokens': 19588}), ToolMessage(content='[{"name":"JAEGER_SAMPLE_RATIO","value":"1"}]', id='f4137cbf-633a-402a-b55c-ff8ac36268cd', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-8afd013124085310'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='45e4ce45-2b71-4c0c-8e65-f338ef3e810c')]]
